meta {
  name: Decide - Task update
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{opaUrl}}/v1/data/umzh/authz/gateway/allow
  body: json
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "input": {
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "path": "/fhir/Task/task-e2e",
        "query": {},
        "headers": {
          "authorization": "Bearer {{bearerToken}}",
          "if-match": "W/\"1\""
        },
        "body": "{\"resourceType\":\"Task\",\"id\":\"task-e2e\",\"status\":\"cancelled\",\"intent\":\"order\",\"requester\":{\"reference\":\"{{orgRef}}\"}}"
      }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  May this caller PUT Task/task-e2e? Requires system/Task.u AND — this is
  DATA-DEPENDENT — the stored Task's requester must equal the token's org, if-match
  its current version, and the body may differ only by a change the Placer may
  make. OPA fetches the Task itself (from its configured fhir_base), so this needs
  the stack up + the Task present. Response: { "result": true|false }.

  After a false, send the same body to .../gateway/status_code: { "result": 412 }
  means a missing or stale if-match.
}
